{
  "title": "Evaluating Palladia® for the Treatment of Canine Oral Melanoma – OVC Clinical Trials",
  "text": "Evaluating Palladia® for the Treatment of Canine Oral Melanoma – OVC Clinical Trials\nSkip to content\nOVC Clinical Trials\nAbout Us\nOur Team\nLocation of Facilities\nSupport Us\nJoin a Study\nCanine Clinical Trials\nFeline Clinical Trials\nLarge Animal Clinical Trials\nResearch Surveys\nResearch\nClinical Trials Superheroes\nResearch Highlights and Publications\nParticipant Stories\nFAQ’s\nContact Us\nOVC Clinical Trials\nToggle Menu\nOVC Clinical Trials\nAbout Us\nOur Team\nLocation of Facilities\nSupport Us\nJoin a Study\nCanine Clinical Trials\nFeline Clinical Trials\nLarge Animal Clinical Trials\nResearch Surveys\nResearch\nClinical Trials Superheroes\nResearch Highlights and Publications\nParticipant Stories\nFAQ’s\nContact Us\nEvaluating Palladia® for the Treatment of Canine Oral Melanoma\nStudy Investigator:\nDr. Anthony Mutsaers\nGraduate Student:\nDr. Gabby Allegrini (DVSc)\nPurpose of the Clinical Study\nPalladia is a type of drug originally used to treat recurrent mast cell tumours in dogs. New evidence has shown that Palladia may be useful for treating other cancer types. Oral melanoma is a locally invasive and highly metastatic cancer. In some cases, even with aggressive therapy, survival times can be as little as 6 months. The use of Palladia, if other treatments have failed, or if traditional therapy is declined, may extend survival in these patients.\nIs Your Pet Eligible?\nDogs with a confirmed diagnosis of oral melanoma through biopsy are eligible. Other specific criteria required to participate include measurable disease, and no previous history of chemotherapy administration. Dogs that have previously received the melanoma vaccine will still be eligible.\nVisits / Samples Required\nMultiple visits to OVC will be required for this study.\nFinancial Incentives\nThe cost of initial staging (blood work, chest x-rays and a biopsy), Palladia medication and associated dispensing and administration fees will be covered by the study.\nU of G 